 "grammar": {
  "title": {
   "ko": "우리 동네 소개 (There is / near / opposite)",
   "en": "Describing my town (There is / near / opposite)"
  },
  "explain": {
   "ko": "동네에 무엇이 있는지는 There is + 단수, There are + 복수로 말합니다. 위치는 near, next to, opposite, far from 등을 씁니다. 동네의 느낌은 be + 형용사로 말합니다: quiet, busy.",
   "en": "Say what is in the area with There is + singular and There are + plural. Place words are near, next to, opposite and far from. Describe the feel of the area with be + adjective: quiet, busy."
  },
  "table": {
   "head": [
    "표현 / Pattern",
    "예 / Example"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "There is + 단수",
     "There is a park."
    ],
    [
     "There are + 복수",
     "There are many restaurants."
    ],
    [
     "opposite / near / far from",
     "The bank is opposite the post office."
    ],
    [
     "be + 형용사",
     "It is quiet."
    ]
   ]
  },
  "notes": [
   {
    "ko": "There is / are는 처음 소개할 때, It is는 이미 아는 것을 말할 때 씁니다.",
    "en": "Use There is / are to introduce things; It is for things already known."
   },
   {
    "ko": "far from 뒤에는 장소를 써요.",
    "en": "After far from use a place."
   },
   {
    "ko": "opposite는 '맞은편에'입니다.",
    "en": "Opposite means across from."
   }
  ],
  "examples": [
   {
    "t": "My neighbourhood is quiet.",
    "ko": "제 동네는 조용해요."
   },
   {
